 "notes": "Wreck plan of the tile wreck (98 x 14.8 m) on the north face of Abu Nuhas, carried in OSM and most guides as the Chrisoula K, here as the Marcus: bow smashed into the reef at 4 m, holds upright with the stacked Italian tiles, stern with the engine room keeled over to starboard at 26-28 m, on a north-east to south-west line. Position and reef edge from OpenStreetMap; dimensions, layout and depths from the Red Sea Wreck Project and dive-guide descriptions; galley, workshop and the route (engine room first, then the holds) from first-hand observation. The Carnatic and the Kimon M are drawn as neighbours; positions are approximate.",
